From: At30c <At30c@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sched/ems: port misfit ratio from the S5E9965

The Exynos 990 EMS judges a task misfit above 80% of the cpu capacity and
a cpu overutilized above 80%, for every task. The S5E9965 EMS makes this
a per-set, per-cpu and per-group ratio (misfit_ratio): a task fits while
its util is below its group's ratio, and a cpu is overutilized above the
lowest ratio of its groups.

Port it as a misfit_ratio emstune node (one value per cpu for each
schedtune group, 0 = 80%) used by the misfit status of the load
balancer, the energy cpu selection and ontime's overutilized source
check. Sets without the node inherit the mode's default set.

As in the S5E9965 normal set, background, root and rt work uses 95% in the
default sets of the everyday modes (normal, power-scenario, light-video,
balance, pinned), so it stays on the smaller cores longer; foreground and
top-app keep 80%, since past the mid cluster comes the Mongoose one (the
S5E9965 uses 70% there). Touch and big boost sets keep 80% everywhere.
cur_set shows the active ratios.
